    <string name="intro_mirror_title">Mirrors</string>
    <string name="intro_mirror_text">Tap a mirror to turn it and bend the beam. Guide the beam into the ring.</string>
    <string name="intro_color_title">Every ring has a colour</string>
    <string name="intro_color_text">A ring lights only with light of its own colour. The dot in the middle shows the colour reaching it now.</string>
    <string name="intro_mix_title">Colours mix</string>
    <string name="intro_mix_text">Two beams meeting in one ring add up: red + green = yellow, red + blue = magenta, green + blue = cyan.</string>
    <string name="intro_split_title">Splitters</string>
    <string name="intro_split_text">A dashed splitter divides the beam in two: one part goes straight on, the other reflects. It turns when tapped, too.</string>
    <string name="intro_filter_title">Filters and white light</string>
    <string name="intro_filter_text">White light is red, green and blue together. Coloured glass lets only its own colour through.</string>
    <string name="intro_portal_title">Portals</string>
    <string name="intro_portal_text">A beam entering a portal comes out of its twin, still heading the same way.</string>
    <string name="intro_oneway_title">One-sided mirrors</string>
    <string name="intro_oneway_text">Only the bright face reflects; the dark back stops the beam. Each tap gives it a quarter turn.</string>

